Subject: Allow native hardware IRQ progress between completed THP video MCUs
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4

Original THPSimple playback invokes the native CPU video decoder synchronously.
Wii hardware continues audio DMA during that work; the native owner needs safe
points to deliver genuine latched interrupts. Opt in through the existing SDK
hardware endpoint after each complete MCU, preserving the decoder parser,
entropy/IDCT/output/restart algorithms and endpoint owner/mask/reentrancy rules.
Default callers retain their decoder policy. This does not guarantee callback
latency across rendering/OS preemption or provide an AX predecessor.

--- a/lib/dolphin/thp/THPDec.cpp
+++ b/lib/dolphin/thp/THPDec.cpp
@@ -1,4 +1,8 @@
 #include "dolphin/thp.h"
+
+#if defined(AURORA_THP_HARDWARE_SAFE_POINTS) && AURORA_THP_HARDWARE_SAFE_POINTS
+#include <aurora/hardware.h>
+#endif
 
 #include "../../internal.hpp"
 
@@ -604,6 +608,14 @@
         return kBadSyntax;
       }
 
+#if defined(AURORA_THP_HARDWARE_SAFE_POINTS) && AURORA_THP_HARDWARE_SAFE_POINTS
+      // The native CPU codec retains the device's independent IRQ progress.
+      // A completed MCU is a stable boundary between entropy/IDCT/output work;
+      // the host endpoint preserves owner, mask and reentrancy rules. No codec
+      // state, equations, source playback decisions or callback are replaced.
+      aurora_service_hardware();
+#endif
